WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:03.844
How AI models run inside your browser tab.

2
00:00:05.344 --> 00:00:10.709
What happens when you press the button in the background remover, upscaler

3
00:00:10.709 --> 00:00:16.147
or transcriber: model downloads, workers, WebGPU and the WebAssembly safety

4
00:00:16.147 --> 00:00:16.437
net.

5
00:00:17.837 --> 00:00:22.980
A model is just a big file. A trained AI model is a file full of numbers,

6
00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:27.629
called weights, plus a description of the math that combines them.

7
00:00:28.929 --> 00:00:33.972
The models behind each tool. Sizes are approximate and depend on the exact

8
00:00:33.972 --> 00:00:36.289
variant, but they give you a feel.

9
00:00:37.589 --> 00:00:41.116
WebGPU first, WebAssembly as the safety net.

10
00:00:41.116 --> 00:00:46.967
WebGPU lets a web page use the graphics card for general math, and neural

11
00:00:46.967 --> 00:00:51.456
networks are mostly the kind of math GPUs are built for.

12
00:00:52.756 --> 00:00:57.869
Why bother doing it this way. Cloud AI tools are fast because they run on

13
00:00:57.869 --> 00:01:01.652
expensive servers, and someone pays for those servers.

14
00:01:02.952 --> 00:01:06.419
To try it, open Background Remover in OpenFile.

15
00:01:06.419 --> 00:01:10.624
Drop in a file, adjust the settings and press the button.

16
00:01:10.624 --> 00:01:14.387
It all runs on your device, so nothing is uploaded.

17
00:01:16.087 --> 00:01:20.375
Read the full post, with live demos, on the OpenFile blog.
